<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02138</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4eb2bcd9-f919-4f9f-a163-1eefb6de71cb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></para>

<para>For questions 1 – 4, solve each equation. Identify every correct answer.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x(3x+12)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=-12\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=-3\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 4\) and \(x=-4\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=-4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = 0\) and \(x=-4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x−7)(x+9)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=7\) and \(x=-7\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\), \(x=7\), and \(x=-9\) </item>
  <item> \(x=7\) and \(x=-9\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-7\) and \(x=9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=7\) and \(x=-9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x−8)(4x+15)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=8\) and \(x=- \frac {15}{4}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=8\) and \(x=-\frac {4}{15}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=8\) and \(x=\frac {4}{15}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=8\) and \(x=\frac {15}{4}\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=8\) and \(x=-\frac {15}{4}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x(x−6)(5x−20)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=0\), \(x=-4\), and \(x=6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\), \(x=4\), and \(x=6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=4\) and \(x=6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=6\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=0\), \(x=4\), and \(x=6\)</para>
<para>For questions 5 - 6, use the following.</para>
<para>The functions below model the height of a projectile in feet, \(t\) seconds after launch.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list>
<item>\(h(t) = -7t^2 + 34t + 48\)</item>
<item>\(h(t) = (-7t − 8)(t − 6)\)</item>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without graphing, determine at what time the height of the object is 0 feet.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(\frac {8}{7}\) seconds </item>
  <item> 6 seconds </item>
  <item> \(-\frac {8}{7}\) seconds </item>
  <item> 0 seconds </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 6 seconds</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Determine the height of the object before it is launched.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> 0 feet </item>
  <item> \(\frac {8}{7}\) feet </item>
  <item> 6 feet </item>
  <item> 48 feet </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 48 feet</para>
<para>For questions 7 – 10, solve each equation. Identify every correct answer.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x(6x−18)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=-3\) </item>
  <item> \(x=3\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=3\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-3\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=0\) and \(x=3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x+13)(x−9)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=-9\) and \(x=-13\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-13\), \(x=0\), and \(x=-9\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-9\) and \(x=13\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-13\) and \(x=9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-13\) and \(x=9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x−7)(x−7)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=7\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-7\) and \(x=7\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=7\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x− \frac {5}{6})(6x+30)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=5\) and \(x=-\frac {5}{6}\) </item>
  <item> \(x=5\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -5\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -6\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -5\) and \(x=\frac {5}{6}\)</para></section>
